Listing 11-8: Testing that a condition will cause a panic!
We place the #[should_panic] attribute after the #[test] attribute and before the test
function it applies to. Let’s look at the result when this test passes:
pub struct Guess {
value: i32,
}
impl Guess {
pub fn new(value: i32) -> Guess {
if value < 1 || value > 100 {
panic!("Guess value must be between 1 and 100, got {value}.");
}
Guess { value }
}
}
#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
use super::*;
#[test]
#[should_panic]
fn greater_than_100() {
Guess::new(200);
}
}
